  Apache 2.0 section 4(a) wants the licence with each copy, so this is the
  SPDX licence list's text.

Weather Icons' OFL.txt is upstream's as served: its copyright lines are the
OFL's unfilled template. Font Logos is the Unlicense (lukas-w/font-logos
1.3.0), which asks for no notice.

Five sets README.md lists as MIT have no licence file under src/glyphs/ at
v3.5.1: Devicons, extraglyphs (Hack), Font Awesome Extension, Seti and
original, and Power Symbols IEC. The texts below are each project's own
notice, fetched 2026-10-23 at the version README.md names where the project
tagged one, and checked against the git blob the GitHub API gives for the
same path at the same ref (blob). The "original" glyphs, the files with
an _nf suffix under src/svgs/ at v3.5.1, name no upstream of their own:
the nerd-fonts repository's LICENSE at that tag puts "Source files not in
folders containing an explicit license" under the MIT licence, Copyright
(c) 2014 Ryan L McIntyre, whose text is the font's LICENSE one directory
up.

